4. Unlicensed Commercial Use — deemed acceptance and remedies

   (a) Acceptance by conduct. By making any Commercial Use of the Software
   without a written agreement with the Licensor, You thereby accept this
   License in its entirety, including this Section 4, by Your conduct alone.
   No notification from You to the Licensor, and no notification from the
   Licensor to You, is required for these terms to bind You. If You do not
   agree to this Section, You must not make Commercial Use of the Software.

   (b) Dual basis. Unlicensed Commercial Use is simultaneously (i) copyright
   infringement, because no license for Commercial Use has been granted, and
   (ii) a breach of the terms accepted under Section 4(a). The Licensor may
   proceed on either basis or both.

   (c) Agreed minimum compensation. For the entire period of Unlicensed
   Commercial Use, You owe the Licensor, as a deemed running royalty and
   agreed minimum compensation — a genuine pre-estimate of the Licensor's
   loss reflecting the default commercial terms in Section 3, and not a
   penalty — an amount equal to no less than thirty percent (30%) of the
   Gross Revenue of each product, service, or offering that made Unlicensed
   Commercial Use of the Software, together with:

      (i)   interest at the applicable statutory rate from the date each
            amount would have fallen due under Section 3; and
      (ii)  the Licensor's costs of enforcement and collection, including
            reasonable attorneys' fees, to the maximum extent permitted by
            applicable law.

   Where the Licensor's provable damages, or the remedies available for
   copyright infringement (including statutory damages where available),
   exceed this minimum, the Licensor may elect the higher amount. Remedies
   under this Section are cumulative with, not in place of, injunctive
   relief and every other remedy available at law or in equity.

   (d) No notice, demand, or cure required. The Licensor may enforce this
   License — including by commencing legal proceedings — at any time and
   without cause shown beyond the Unlicensed Commercial Use itself, without
   prior notice, warning, demand, or opportunity to cure, and without any
   obligation to first offer or negotiate a commercial agreement. Any cure
   period in Section 7 (Termination) applies only to Noncommercial Use and
   does not limit this Section.

   (e) Records and audit. If You make Commercial Use of the Software, You
   must keep complete and accurate records sufficient to determine the Gross
   Revenue of each product, service, or offering concerned, and retain them
   for at least six (6) years. On fourteen (14) days' written notice, and
   not more than once per calendar year absent discovered underpayment, the
   Licensor (or an independent auditor bound to confidentiality) may audit
   those records. If an audit reveals a shortfall exceeding five percent
   (5%), You bear the reasonable cost of the audit in addition to the
   shortfall.

   (f) No waiver. The Licensor's delay or failure to enforce this License
   against You or anyone else is not a waiver of any right and does not
